{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"find /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src -name guide.md -o -name behavior-facts.md -o -name audit.md; sed -n '969,987p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '825,921p' ../agent-source/internal/rsm/statemachine.go; sed -n '90,126p' ../agent-source/internal/raft/entryutils.go; sed -n '649,669p' ../agent-source/internal/raft/raft.go\"","aggregated_output":"\treturn isLocalMessageType(t)\n}\n\nfunc isLocalMessageType(t pb.MessageType) bool {\n\treturn t == pb.Election ||\n\t\tt == pb.LeaderHeartbeat ||\n\t\tt == pb.Unreachable ||\n\t\tt == pb.SnapshotStatus ||\n\t\tt == pb.CheckQuorum ||\n\t\tt == pb.LocalTick ||\n\t\tt == pb.BatchedReadIndex\n}\n\nfunc isResponseMessageType(t pb.MessageType) bool {\n\treturn t == pb.ReplicateResp ||\n\t\tt == pb.RequestVoteResp ||\n\t\tt == pb.HeartbeatResp ||\n\t\tt == pb.ReadIndexResp ||\n\t\tt == pb.Unreachable ||\n\t\tt == pb.SnapshotStatus ||\n\t\tt == pb.LeaderTransfer\n}\nfunc (r *raft) finalizeMessageTerm(m pb.Message) pb.Message {\n\tif m.Term == 0 && m.Type == pb.RequestVote {\n\t\tplog.Panicf(\"%s sending RequestVote with 0 term\", r.describe())\n\t}\n\tif m.Term > 0 && m.Type != pb.RequestVote {\n\t\tplog.Panicf(\"%s term unexpectedly set for message type %d\",\n\t\t\tr.describe(), m.Type)\n\t}\n\tif !isRequestMessage(m.Type) {\n\t\tm.Term = r.term\n\t}\n\treturn m\n}\n\nfunc (r *raft) send(m pb.Message) {\n\tm.From = r.nodeID\n\tm = r.finalizeMessageTerm(m)\n\tr.msgs = append(r.msgs, m)\n}\n\nfunc (r *raft) sendRateLimitMessage() {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/behavior-facts.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/behavior-facts.md'","aggregated_output":"# Investigation and selection\n\nCandidate investigates a sourced question, including unknown requirements, protection premises or legal history. Obligation fixes an applicable responsibility without presuming violation; Check supplies inputs, history and observations. Missing authority calls for contract investigation, missing history for source work or conditional exploration. Neither gap bars a Candidate or licenses an invented obligation.\n\nFirst explain both core relationships from activity_roles and their connection in AuditSpec.core_overview. Follow representative work through owners, qualified support, aggregation, decision, propagation and consumption; explain acquisition, change and loss of context/authority and handling of old requests, replies, pending support and established decisions. Read the supporting membership, history, recovery and completion mechanisms needed for this backbone. Trace callers and callees, important rejection, retry and asynchronous paths; deeper variants may remain open.\n\nSave early discrepancies as sourced Surfaces or specific unknowns even when no obligation is ready. Distinguish open_details from core_gaps: unexplained formation, authority transition or old-work handling breaks readiness; a usable overview can retain local anomalies. Only a preconfigured directed_question permits a proportionate local boundary first; activity_focus does not. A usable map and first Candidate may share a product. Unmapped source work and exploration need no fabricated Fact.\n\nUse behavior-facts.md for implementation meaning. Select a principal Fact lifecycle with a sourced A1/A2 connection; a question need not span both. Direct behavior_ids establish, consume, invalidate or reinterpret it; supporting_behavior_ids explain separate history/context/consequence support. Cross-activity effects establish actual relationships without relabeling support Activities. Names and protocol labels establish neither relevance nor responsibility.\n\nUse question, counterevidence, unknowns, importance and trigger_rationale to identify what remains unexplained, what existing protection does establish, and what the next action will distinguish. A concise sourced difference suffices; no ranking, mandatory alternative list or confidence threshold. Compare contract reading, smaller exploration and another known relationship before committing to a costly test. “This input has not been run” alone is not a discriminator. An empty unknowns list does not disqualify a check whose earlier investigation established its value.\n\nWhen the actual mechanism explains the suspicion and no important execution premise remains, use explained or sourced feedback and reselect without manufacturing a Unit. An explicit guard with unresolved ownership, timing, producer or context instead calls for investigation of that premise. A negative result should identify the plausible explanation it excluded and independent premises left open; distinguish it from execution corroborating an already-explained protection. Neither settles the entire Fact or becomes a reason to expand input variants indefinitely. Keep one requirement's independent scenarios together; a genuinely different responsibility gets its own question.\n\nConditional differences with unclear contracts remain exploration or local pause. Once responsibility is grounded, obligation and construction may be separate products. Reuse helpers and legal prefixes only after checking their entry, caller duties, completion order and fault assumptions for this question. A convenient driver must not exclude permitted overlap that supplied the discriminator, nor assume a looser ordering is legal because it produces a difference. Fixed checks must still exercise the investigated premise; a narrower child cannot settle its parent. Use existing F2/F3 when requirement or scope changes. Finish necessary technical repair and review of accepted work; switching questions preserves its debt.\n\nPrioritize consensus safety and explicitly scoped progress duties. Distinguish a sourced numeric/event deadline, implementation-owned automatic continuation without a numeric deadline, and later work explicitly owed by the caller. No numeric deadline does not preclude investigating lost continuation triggers; the word automatic alone supplies no obligation. A possible later event in a comment is not a guarantee that callers produce it. Independently grounded eligibility, accounting, wakeup or correlation duties can be resolved without a client endpoint or global consequence. Shared facts and helpers transfer understanding, not results.\n\nAt handoffs identify the answered proposition, supporting sources/execution and independent remaining question in feedback. At the next substantive product already updating the relevant Behavior, Fact or overview, or preparing a Candidate that relies on that knowledge, replace the answered original sentence with its sourced conditional relationship and remove obsolete execution/review reminders. Preserve independent unknowns and historical inputs. Consult the actual answer and assessment; an understanding label or exact reference does not establish resolution. Correct misleading explanations before reuse, without a dedicated cleanup turn or unrelated whole-map sweep. Source reading and exploration may continue from feedback; near expiry save minimal complete learning. Use behavior-facts.md for field ownership and tasks/audit.md for product references.\n\nOpen runs continue investigation until controller time/call or actual interruption boundaries. Empty pending_work or disposed registered questions does not exhaust the frontier: use the overview, other consumers/contexts, Surfaces and unread paths. Execution, Unit, review or revision limits restrict those actions, not remaining authorized source work. Near expiry take a smaller informative step; do not reset budgets, repeat empty work or sleep to fill time. Only a preconfigured finite directed task may complete early. Actual cancellation, safety refusal, permission loss and unrecoverable service/tool failure still stop.\n# Conditions, effects and semantic facts\n\nDescribe sourced owners, triggers, guards, state changes, effects and asynchronous boundaries. For a relevant relationship already read, identify who establishes the fact under which conditions and what its consumer actually requires. Include other read establishment, invalidation or reinterpretation paths; unread paths remain unknown or sourced Surfaces.\n\nShared updates do not imply shared follow-up effects. When one entry establishes a fact and schedules a consumer but another only establishes the fact, preserve that distinction in trigger, important_branches, writes, external_effects or async_boundaries. Do not union effects into an unconditional guarantee. Distinguish possible effects, conditional scheduling and guaranteed completion. A Behavior can cover multiple entries when conditions remain clear; split minimally when owners, completion boundaries or meanings cannot be expressed accurately together. Do not enumerate every branch or duplicate a shared Fact.\n\nFact states the assertion actually established for its identity and validity_context, not the strongest effect seen on any path. Reporting, internal accounting, notification and completed external work are distinct. Trace relevant guard inputs to their producer, update point, owner and completion duty instead of trusting a variable name. Conversely, a missing local field is not a missing guarantee when dispatch, admission, serialization or reset supplies it. Assess the composed producer/consumer protection, not each structure in isolation. Absent direct action is a question: inspect alternative consumers, delayed validation, shared scheduling and recovery for the same object and history before alleging a defect.\n\nUse produces_fact_ids/consumes_fact_ids for established relationships needed by later questions; reverse indexes are derived. No name-based edges, mandatory edges, branch fields or completeness scores. Reference validation proves structure, not equivalent path meaning. Guards and observed differences do not supply normative obligations without applicable sources and reasoning.\n\nUse existing map_changes at natural handoffs. Correcting an overstrong abstraction challenges the specific Candidate premise that depended on it; independent results retain their original basis. Use preserves only when requirements, dependencies and observation scope actually remain applicable. Meaning, identity, context and dependency changes cannot masquerade as clarification. No change means no version; keep history and counterevidence.\n\nKeep Fact meaning, identity and validity_context about the assertion established, not the full explanation of a Candidate. Put newly understood producer guards, retry branches, notifications and completion duties in Behavior, including field changes that schedule no follow-up. At a related handoff remove only the answered unknown and retain independent gaps; an explained Candidate needs no new challenge merely to restate its protection. If that protection or the Fact's actual context changes, attribute the challenge even when the Candidate was explained. Candidate/feedback owns the scoped disposition, Scope owns exclusions, and CheckRun/assessment owns execution/review progress. Name unresolved semantic premises instead of process reminders. Surface.reason is a reading question; mapped means association, not resolution. Map and map_changes source_ids cite Material ranges; experiment identities stay in feedback and fixed artifacts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_map.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nold=json.load(open('submission.json'))\nsources=old['sources']\ndef src(i,f,a,b,k='code_observation'):\n sources.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k)); return i\nsrc('S-log','internal/raft/logentry.go',290,399)\nsrc('S-recovery','internal/raft/raft.go',237,292)\nsrc('S-snapshot','internal/raft/raft.go',437,529)\nsrc('S-ticks','internal/raft/raft.go',559,630)\nsrc('S-replication-send','internal/raft/raft.go',718,813)\nsrc('S-replication-recv','internal/raft/raft.go',1316,1391)\nsrc('S-transfer','internal/raft/raft.go',1742,1769)\nsrc('S-follower-read','internal/raft/raft.go',1936,1984)\nsrc('S-check-quorum','internal/raft/raft.go',1603,1614)\nsrc('S-node-config','node.go',254,333)\nsrc('S-node-replay','node.go',623,649)\nsrc('S-node-effects','node.go',969,1004)\nsrc('S-node-updates','node.go',1058,1103)\nsrc('S-node-read','node.go',1225,1234)\nsrc('S-client-batches','request.go',823,938)\nsrc('S-client-expiry','request.go',939,965)\nsrc('S-rsm-config','internal/rsm/statemachine.go',960,975)\nsrc('S-rsm-recovery','internal/rsm/statemachine.go',243,259)\nsrc('S-rsm-restore','internal/rsm/statemachine.go',324,375)\nsrc('S-member-guards','internal/rsm/membership.go',113,304)\nsrc('S-rsm-apply','internal/rsm/statemachine.go',825,919)\nsrc('S-rsm-work','internal/rsm/statemachine.go',547,599)\nsrc('S-node-applied','node.go',238,252)\nsrc('S-read-api','nodehost.go',855,870,'interface_statement')\nsrc('S-peer-read','internal/raft/peer.go',284,307)\nsrc('S-message-term','internal/raft/raft.go',649,667)\nsrc('S-message-types','internal/raft/entryutils.go',103,111)\nbeh=[]\ndef b(i,a,owner,ctx,trigger,ss,**kw):\n beh.append(dict(id=i,primary_activity=a,execution_owner=owner,protocol_context=ctx,trigger=trigger,source_ids=ss,**kw))\nb('B-formation','A1','raft leader and followers','cluster, leader term, log index and configured voting members','Propose appends entries; Replicate and ReplicateResp advance matching history.', ['S-formation','S-log','S-read-consume','S-replication-send','S-replication-recv','S-quorum'],implementation_guards=['Only leader handles proposals; leader transfer drops proposals.','Follower checks predecessor term and refuses conflicting committed entries.','Commit quorum counts full members plus witnesses, excludes observers, and requires current-term entry at the quorum index.'],writes=['Leader stamps entry term/index and updates own match.','Accepted responses monotonically advance remote match; successful commitment broadcasts replication.'],important_branches=['Reject response decreases next and retries; paused progress resumes via responses.','Compacted history may send snapshot only to an active remote.','Witness replication carries metadata except configuration changes.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-committed'],async_boundaries=['Messages are queued for node/engine transport and persistence.'])\nb('B-authority','A2','raft state machine through Peer.Handle','cluster term, role, vote and membership','Ticks, vote requests/replies, higher-term messages, quorum checks and leadership transfer.', ['S-formation','S-term','S-peer-admission','S-message-types','S-ticks','S-transfer','S-follower-read','S-check-quorum'],implementation_guards=['Unknown response senders are rejected by Peer.Handle; candidate separately rejects observers.','Votes are unique by sender and require log freshness on grant.','Election blocked when committed entries remain unapplied; removed nodes do not campaign on tick.','Lower-term messages discarded; recent-leader check may reject a higher-term vote request.'],writes=['Candidacy increments term and self-votes; majority promotes leader and appends no-op.','Reset clears votes, remote match, pending readIndex, transfer and pending-config flag; leader promotion scans uncommitted configuration entries.'],important_branches=['Higher-term traffic changes role/context except protected recent-leader vote requests.','CheckQuorum loss and local removal relinquish leadership.','Transfer targets a full member caught up to last index, sends TimeoutNow; transfer timeout aborts.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-committed'],external_effects=['Pending requests can be dropped by role handlers; old replicated log remains subject to new leader matching, not cleared by reset.'])\nb('B-membership','A4','RSM membership and node.ApplyConfigChange','committed configuration entry and current membership','RSM applies configuration entry and calls node to update raft and routing.', ['S-rsm-config','S-member-guards','S-node-config','S-membership'],implementation_guards=['Ordered mode checks ConfigChangeId; removed IDs cannot be added again.','Full members cannot demote to observer/witness; witness promotion disallowed; observer promotion requires same address.','Leader permits one pending configuration proposal and substitutes no-op for another.'],writes=['Accepted RSM membership is reflected in raft membership; rejected change clears pending flag.','Removing leader steps down; removing a peer recomputes commit when still leader.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Changes quorum population and replication destinations.','A2':'Changes eligibility and may revoke local leadership.'},source_ids_extra=[])\nbeh[-1].pop('source_ids_extra'); beh[-1]['source_ids'].append('S-read-consume')\nb('B-persistence','A6','engine worker, node and logdb','per-cluster updates and persisted term/vote/log','Engine gathers Peer updates, saves Raft state, sends effects and commits update acknowledgment.', ['S-engine-order','S-node-effects','S-node-updates','S-node-replay','S-recovery','S-peer-read'],important_branches=['Replicate and Ping may be sent before SaveRaftState; other messages, including vote/replication responses, are sent afterward.','Committed entries may use FastApply; this is distinct from persistence acknowledgment.'],durable_effects=['SaveRaftState persists gathered state and entries through configured logdb.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Orders durable acknowledgment of replication support.','A2':'Recovered state restores term and vote.'},unknowns=['Specific logdb crash/atomicity behavior and FastApply variants remain untraced.'])\nb('B-recovery','A3','raft, node snapshot handling and RSM','snapshot index/term/membership plus persisted state','Log replay at startup or accepted InstallSnapshot followed by RSM recovery.', ['S-snapshot','S-node-replay','S-recovery','S-rsm-recovery','S-rsm-restore','S-node-config','S-log','S-node-updates'],implementation_guards=['Snapshot not newer than commit rejected; matching snapshot index/term advances commit without replacing log.','Role conversion constraints guard snapshot restore.','RSM rejects out-of-date recovery and restores remotes after recovery succeeds.'],writes=['Log restore sets committed and processed to snapshot index.','RSM restores membership/applied index and callbacks rebuild remote progress.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-committed'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Restores committed prefix and replication progress context.','A2':'Restores participant identities; self-removal can revoke leadership.'})\nb('B-apply','A5','RSM apply worker and node callbacks','ordered committed entries and client operation identifiers','Node queues committed entries; RSM handles entries and updates applied state.', ['S-rsm-apply','S-rsm-work','S-node-applied','S-node-updates'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-committed'],writes=['Configuration entries update membership; session-managed commands update application and invoke ApplyUpdate.'],external_effects=['Proposal completion correlates client/series/key; qualifying ApplyUpdate also advances pending read completion.'],async_boundaries=['RSM task queue separates commitment from application; processed work signals StepReady.'],unknowns=['Session replay/deduplication and on-disk state-machine variants need deeper tracing.'])\nb('B-read-admit','A2','raft leader','leader term, SystemCtx and request origin','ReadIndex handler requires current-term commit for multi-voter quorum, stores context and sends heartbeat probes.', ['S-read-consume','S-read-send','S-read-queue','S-quorum'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-committed'],produces_fact_ids=['F-pending-read'],implementation_guards=['Witness origin rejected; duplicate context does not add another queue entry.','Nonzero contexts sent only to voting members; observers receive only zero-context ordinary heartbeats.'],important_branches=['Single-voter quorum produces local readiness immediately and can send response to observer origin.','Multi-voter leader without current-term commit reports dropped request.'],external_effects=['Pending latest context is retransmitted on heartbeat ticks.'])\nb('B-read-confirm','A2','raft leader heartbeat-response handler and readIndex','pending context in current leadership generation','Known-member heartbeat response with nonzero Hint calls confirm; distinct sender confirmations plus leader are compared with quorum.', ['S-read-queue','S-read-response','S-read-consume','S-dispatch','S-peer-admission'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-pending-read'],produces_fact_ids=['F-confirmed-read'],writes=['A confirmed queue prefix is removed and returned; each returned status retains its origin and context and receives latest confirmed index.'],external_effects=['Local status uses s.ctx for readiness; remote response uses s.from and s.index but triggering message Hint/HintHigh.'],unknowns=['Whether remote queue-prefix responses preserve each request context under overlapping remote requests.'])\nb('B-read-deliver','A2','leader response emitter and follower response handler','originating node and full SystemCtx','Leader consumes confirmed statuses; follower processes term-admitted ReadIndexResp.', ['S-read-response','S-follower-read','S-term','S-peer-admission'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-confirmed-read'],external_effects=['Remote response becomes ReadyToRead with received context/index; follower marks leader available.'],unknowns=['Distinct remote contexts can be emitted under one trigger context; exact endpoint effects need a legal execution.'])\nb('B-read-client','A7','node and pendingReadIndex','local batch SystemCtx and RequestState deadline','Node batches incoming reads with generated context; ReadyToRead and applied callbacks complete matching batches.', ['S-node-read','S-client-batches','S-client-expiry','S-node-updates','S-node-applied','S-read-api','S-peer-read'],writes=['Each batch is keyed by complete SystemCtx; addReady changes only exact-key batch index.'],external_effects=['Nonzero batch index at or below applied completes unexpired requests; expired requests time out.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Consumes leadership-confirmed read context; does not interpret later contexts as covering different local batches.','A5':'Read completion additionally waits for application through the returned index.'},unknowns=['End-to-end timeout and retry consequences of response-context mismatch remain unexecuted.'])\nfacts=[dict(id='F-committed',meaning='Local log committed index denotes the prefix selected as committed by term-qualified leader quorum, accepted leader commitment, recovered durable state or snapshot.',identity={'cluster':'clusterID','prefix':'committed index'},validity_context='Local raft history and current recovered/configured context; commitment is distinct from persisted/appplied completion.',representation=['entryLog.committed'],durability='Persisted through engine update protocol; an in-memory assignment alone is not durable acknowledgment.',recovery='loadState restores commit; snapshot restore establishes snapshot prefix.',source_ids=['S-formation','S-log','S-replication-recv','S-recovery','S-snapshot']),dict(id='F-pending-read',meaning='Leader has registered a read origin and context with a committed index and queued it for heartbeat confirmation.',identity={'cluster':'clusterID','context':'SystemCtx High and Low','origin':'readStatus.from'},validity_context='Current leader readIndex instance; unique context until confirm removal or authority reset.',representation=['readIndex.pending','readIndex.queue'],durability='Volatile',recovery='Not recovered; reset replaces readIndex.',invalidators=['B-authority','B-read-confirm'],source_ids=['S-read-consume','S-read-queue','S-formation']),dict(id='F-confirmed-read',meaning='readIndex.confirm returned a status from the prefix ending at the context whose distinct sender confirmations plus leader meet the supplied quorum; status retains its own origin/context and receives the confirming status index.',identity={'cluster':'clusterID','context':'readStatus.ctx','origin':'readStatus.from'},validity_context='Returned statuses in one leader confirmation handler invocation, with caller supplying current quorum and accepted heartbeat sender.',representation=['[]*readStatus returned by confirm'],durability='Transient, not persisted',recovery='No reconstruction; pending state is reset on role transition.',source_ids=['S-read-queue','S-read-response','S-read-consume'])]\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nacts=[]\nfor a in roles:\n bs=[x for x in beh if x['primary_activity']==a]\n acts.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=roles[a]['relation'],realization_summary=' '.join(x['trigger'] for x in bs),entry_points=[x['execution_owner'] for x in bs],source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(z for x in bs for z in x['source_ids']))))\nover=dict(status='usable',rationale='Representative formation and authority paths, their history/membership coupling and application boundaries are traced. Local questions and variants remain open; this is not coverage or correctness certification.',formation=dict(explanation='Node/Peer proposals reach the leader, which appends current-term entries and sends predecessor-qualified replication. Followers reject mismatching prefixes or append matching entries, protect committed history and acknowledge accepted indexes. Engine persists ordinary responses before sending them (replication requests may precede persistence). Leader aggregates full-member and witness match values, selects the quorum index and commits only a current-term entry there, thereby carrying its prefix. Commit is propagated in replication/heartbeat messages; committed entries pass through a separate RSM queue to membership/application processing and client callbacks. Rejections retry with lower next; compacted histories use snapshots for active peers.',behavior_ids=['B-formation','B-persistence','B-apply','B-recovery'],fact_ids=['F-committed'],source_ids=['S-formation','S-log','S-replication-send','S-replication-recv','S-engine-order','S-node-effects','S-rsm-apply']),context=dict(explanation='Election ticks on eligible full members trigger term increment and self-vote. Vote grants require vote eligibility and log freshness; known response admission and unique sender counting qualify election support. Promotion resets progress and adds a current-term no-op. Higher-term messages normally relinquish authority; stale terms are rejected, with a recent-leader exception for higher-term vote requests. Configured quorum checks revoke inactive leadership. Transfer pauses proposals, waits for a full target to catch up and sends TimeoutNow; timeout cancels transfer. Reset drops volatile pending reads and votes while retaining log history. Application of removal revokes local leadership; restart restores persisted term/vote/commit and snapshot membership.',behavior_ids=['B-authority','B-membership','B-recovery','B-persistence'],source_ids=['S-formation','S-term','S-peer-admission','S-ticks','S-transfer','S-check-quorum','S-membership','S-recovery']),connection=dict(explanation='Only support qualified by current term/role and current membership advances formation; remote progress is rebuilt on authority reset while committed log history constrains future leaders through freshness and prefix checks. Pending configuration entries limit new proposals, and committed-but-unapplied work suppresses campaigning to avoid stale membership authority. RSM accepts legal configuration transitions then updates raft quorum membership. ReadIndex separately confirms current leadership only after current-term commitment, probes voting members and resolves a queued prefix; application and exact request context determine client completion. Old nonzero-term replies are filtered, pending read support is discarded on reset, and old log entries remain recoverable rather than being treated as current quorum proof.',behavior_ids=['B-formation','B-authority','B-membership','B-read-admit','B-read-confirm','B-read-deliver','B-read-client'],fact_ids=['F-committed','F-pending-read','F-confirmed-read'],source_ids=['S-term','S-formation','S-membership','S-rsm-config','S-read-consume','S-read-queue','S-read-response','S-client-batches']),open_details=['Remote read-index queue-prefix response context and request correlation.','Read confirmation support spanning membership changes; legal schedules and retained confirmations need investigation.','Logdb crash atomicity, session replay and on-disk state-machine variants remain local unread details.'],core_gaps=[])\nm=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Dragonboat Go module: node/engine, internal Raft, RSM, storage and client-facing read completion; network, storage backend and application boundaries are implementation interfaces, not assumed correct.',protocol_contexts=['Per-cluster term/role/log/membership','ReadIndex SystemCtx and node-local request batches'],ownership=['Raft state machine owns election, replication and read confirmation; engine coordinates persistence/transport; RSM owns application and membership acceptance.'],variants=['Full voting node','Non-voting observer','Voting metadata witness','In-memory, concurrent and on-disk application state machines'],source_ids=['S-quorum','S-recovery','S-rsm-apply','S-read-api']),activities=acts,behaviors=beh,facts=facts,core_overview=over,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='raft.handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-read-confirm','B-read-deliver'],reason='Why do remote responses use the triggering context while confirmed statuses retain distinct contexts?',source_ids=['S-read-response','S-read-queue'],high_consequence=False),dict(entry_point='raft.handleNodeConfigChange/readIndex.confirm',disposition='deferred',reason='Determine which pending confirmation support remains eligible across legal membership changes.',source_ids=['S-membership','S-read-queue'],high_consequence=True)])\njson.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='When a later heartbeat context confirms a prefix containing distinct remote read requests, does response propagation preserve the origin and context of each returned status, as required by exact-context completion at the requester?',importance='Mis-correlation can discard a completed authority check for an earlier admitted remote read and cause avoidable timeout; no stale-read or whole-cluster liveness consequence is established.',source_ids=['S-read-queue','S-read-response','S-follower-read','S-client-batches','S-node-read','S-read-api'],participants=['Leader','Two remote read-origin nodes','Voting heartbeat responders'],objects=['readStatus','SystemCtx','ReadIndexResp','node-local read batch'],contexts=['Stable term and membership','Distinct pending read contexts','Latest context reaches quorum before an earlier context'],event_paths=['node.handleReadIndex -> Peer.ReadIndex -> follower forwarding -> leader queue -> heartbeat confirmation -> remote response -> follower readiness -> exact batch lookup'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B-read-confirm','B-read-deliver'],fact_ids=['F-confirmed-read'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-read-admit':'Registers actual request context and sends probes after current-term commit.','B-read-client':'Exact-key consumer establishes relevance of preserving each context.','B-authority':'Term and role admission constrain a legal schedule.','B-persistence':'Peer driver must honor state/message persistence ordering.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Local-origin returned statuses use s.ctx correctly.','Duplicate context admission is coalesced, so distinct contexts are necessary.','Timeout remains a permitted client outcome; this question concerns response correlation, not a numeric success deadline.'],unknowns=['Find an applicable per-request correlation responsibility and determine whether a latest-context remote response has any alternative completion interpretation.','Construct a legal Peer-level history with current-term commit and overlapping remote reads, retaining actual heartbeat provenance.'],trigger_rationale='The producer returns each status with its own ctx, but remote emission substitutes m.Hint/m.HintHigh while follower and pendingReadIndex consume exact received context. Contract/source reading has narrowed the discrepancy; a bounded legal schedule is more discriminating than arbitrary malformed messages or additional observer variants.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nsub=dict(action='continue',rationale='Register usable two-core overview and select the sourced read-context consumption discrepancy for responsibility and legal-history investigation.',map_path='map.json',sources=sources,question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S-read-response','S-read-queue','S-client-batches','S-node-read','S-member-guards'],answered='Follower read completion is exact-context: node batches independently generated SystemCtx values and pendingReadIndex.addReady updates only a matching map key. Thus remote queue-prefix propagation is not explained by a generic latest-context completion rule. Legal RSM membership transitions also prohibit full-member demotion and re-adding removed IDs, constraining the earlier observer eligibility suspic